In his article, gordon@osiris.cso.uiuc.edu (John Gordon) writes :

>	---Jedi Knight??  Tell me more!

Well, you asked for it !

A long, long time ago, in a computer game far, far away...
(Actually that was NetHack 2.3)

The 'YODA' stuff was my very first hack in Hack ;-)

It added a new class (the Jedi Knight) and a set of objects that implemented
the concept of the 'laser saber'.
Basically the 'light sword' comes to life only when you wield it (cute? message
here). It's a really good sword (cuts in armor like a hot knife in butter)
but has its drawbacks : you have to feed it with batteries (rare and expensive)
and it has some bad side-effects in some situations (intended to be
discovered by the player at his depends <evil grin>).

Another drawback : it was buggy (sigh)! (my *FIRST* hack, remember)

In the very beginning of 3.0 the devteam decided to limit anachronisms since
we wanted to be as close as possible to the spirit of Fantasy RPG.
So, exit the 'YODA' patches (no real regrets).

That's the story...

So long,

